=== Prompt ===
Who is Lara Croft?

=== Response ===
Lara Croft is a fictional character and the protagonist of the Square Enix's "Tomb Raider" video game franchise. She was created by Toby Gard, Kirk Anderson, and Jeremy Heath-Smith, and designed by artist Alex West, with the first game in the series being released in 1996.

Lara Croft is an English archaeologist who is known for her acrobatic and athletic skills, intelligence, and physical attractiveness. She's often depicted as adventurous, fearless, and resourceful, with a strong will and determination. Lara Croft has been portrayed by various actors in movies and TV shows, most notably by Angelina Jolie in the "Lara Croft: Tomb Raider" film series.

The "Tomb Raider" series is one of the best-selling video game franchises of all time, and Lara Croft is considered an icon of video game culture and a cultural icon in her own right.

